/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    Written to attack the copy of a text stored where a body cannot see how long the target
    lives (2026-11-17 review): text field set through param object method chain (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Define object box with (the text tag).
Define object shelf with (the series of box boxes).
Bind void to retag-first unto shelf, given (the text t):
    Define first as item 1 of one's boxes.
    first's tag becomes t joined to "!".
    Item 1 of one's boxes becomes first.
Done.
Define wall as a new shelf { the boxes (a series of box) }.
Insert (a new box { the tag "outer" }) into wall's boxes.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast wall's retag-first on ("in" joined to "ner").
Done.

Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State (item 1 of wall's boxes)'s tag.
